drumee-server-pod (2.9.74) stable; urgency=medium

  * Fix the systemd unit killing the processes it starts. ExecStart hands off to
    pm2 and returns, and with the default RemainAfterExit=no systemd treated that
    as the service having finished, then tore down the cgroup — taking the pm2
    daemon with it. So "systemctl start drumee-server-pod" never worked and the
    stack did not come up after a reboot, while running the same init script from
    a shell did, because it landed outside the unit's cgroup. Now oneshot with
    RemainAfterExit=yes.
  * Depend on drumee-node-runtime, which supplies pm2. The init script invokes pm2
    by name and nothing installed it, so a fresh install reported every package
    installed and served nothing, failing with "pm2: command not found". Debian
    ships no pm2 package. Note this pulls in nodejs (>= 22) transitively, which
    Trixie cannot satisfy alone; scripts/baremetal.sh configures NodeSource before
    installing.

 -- Somanos Sar <somanos.sar@drumee.com>  Fri, 31 Jul 2026 16:33:43 +0200

